WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.260
If C-tactile input makes a stroke feel pleasant, what happens when that input is

2
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:09.260
taken away?

3
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:13.133
No one can remove a fibre class from a healthy person.

4
00:00:13.673 --> 00:00:16.353
But some people have lost part of their touch pathway.

5
00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.867
Start with the reverse case.

6
00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:24.727
In 2002, Olausson and colleagues studied a patient lacking large myelinated

7
00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:25.727
afferents.

8
00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:30.547
Stroking that excites C-tactile afferents produced a faint, pleasant sensation.

9
00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:37.217
Imaging showed insular activation, and none detectable in primary or secondary

10
00:00:37.217 --> 00:00:38.577
somatosensory cortex.

11
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.400
One patient shows what this input can do without large fibres, not that it is

12
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.400
needed.

13
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:51.243
Next, ten carriers of a nerve growth factor mutation They have fewer thin and

14
00:00:51.243 --> 00:00:52.303
unmyelinated fibres.

15
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:58.613
Predict. How should they rate slow stroking at the speeds C-tactile afferents

16
00:00:58.613 --> 00:00:59.613
prefer?

17
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:07.363
They rated it less pleasant than matched controls.

18
00:01:08.283 --> 00:01:11.843
And their posterior insula was not modulated by that stroking.

19
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:17.617
The mutation affects more than C-tactile afferents, so this is not a clean removal.

20
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.600
Now cut a route instead.

21
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.760
An anterolateral cordotomy cuts part of the spinal cord to relieve intractable pain.

22
00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:35.803
In 2019, Marshall and colleagues tested such patients before and after, with a brush

23
00:01:35.803 --> 00:01:36.803
at three speeds.

24
00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:41.353
Predict. Pain and temperature travel in that tract.

25
00:01:42.253 --> 00:01:45.153
If pleasant touch travelled only there, what should the cut do?

26
00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:54.137
Pain, temperature and itch were markedly disrupted.

27
00:01:54.137 --> 00:01:57.937
But pleasantness ratings were not significantly changed.

28
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:04.537
With 19 patients, that is not proof of no change.

29
00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:06.757
But the ratings did not vanish.

30
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.340
The authors proposed a route outside that tract, most likely the dorsal columns.

31
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.463
So the two tests ask different questions.

32
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:20.663
With fewer thin fibres, carriers rated caress-speed stroking as less pleasant.

33
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:24.643
Cordotomy cut one route, yet pleasantness survived.

34
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:28.703
Neither test shows which fibres carry the surviving signal.

35
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:33.923
So thin-fibre input seems to contribute, and this route is not needed.

36
00:02:34.883 --> 00:02:38.043
C-tactile input remains a candidate, its route unresolved.
